  <entry>
    <id>https://doi.org/10.1002/sej.70056</id>
    <title>New wine, old bottles? Effective strategies of new
                    &lt;scp&gt;GenAI&lt;/scp&gt;
                    firms</title>
    <updated>2026-10-12T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Kathleen M. Eisenhardt, Xilan Zhang</name>
    </author>
    <content>&lt;b&gt;Strategic Entrepreneurship Journal&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;Blending insights from GenAI, strategic reasoning, and empirical grounding in five illustrative ventures, we contribute a theoretical framework for effective strategies of new GenAI firms. They facebifurcated uncertainty(i.e., high uncertainty of a nascent market, moderate uncertainty of a somewhat predictable technology trajectory) such that twocomplementary strategic logics—Process Perspective (PP) and Resource‐based View (RBV)—are relevant. Second, we identifyprocess‐based(i.e., well‐designed business model and product innovation process) andresource‐based(i.e., superior data, efficient orchestration, complementary resources) advantages. Some relate to GenAI, some generalize. Third, we address what is unique about GenAI entrepreneurship, includingstrategic implicationsof GenAI,technology strategywhen there is upstream technical dominance and many downstream firms, and across‐technology comparisonwith technologies like software and predictive AI.Managerial SummaryThe rapid trajectory of GenAI is stunning. Yet many new GenAI firms are simply thin wrappers around well‐known LLMs. Drawing on five illustrative ventures, we contribute a framework for effective strategies for new GenAI firms. These firms facebifurcated uncertainty(i.e., high uncertainty of a nascent market, moderate uncertainty of a somewhat predictable technology trajectory). This calls for creating advantage by navigating high uncertainty markets to accomplish key strategic tasks and relying on foresight to build strategically valuable resources. Specifically, we identifyprocess‐based(well‐designed business model and product innovation process) andresource‐based(i.e., superior data, efficient orchestration, complementary resources) advantages. We also address what is unique about GenAI entrepreneurship, includingstrategic implicationsof GenAI and across‐technology comparisonwith technologies like software, predictive AI, and quantum.</content>
